Subject: [PATCH 17/17] 68040: the fault address is the first byte of the
 faulted access

MC68040UM 8.4.6.4: "For a misaligned access that faults, the FA field
contains the address of the first byte of the transfer, regardless of which
of the two or three bus transfers for the misaligned access was faulted",
and WB3A tells a handler where to complete the write-back (8.4.6.5). A bus
error raised by the host on the second word of a long word stacked the
address of that word, so a handler completing WB3 wrote the long word two
bytes too far.
---
 Moira/MoiraDataflow_cpp.h | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Moira/MoiraDataflow_cpp.h b/Moira/MoiraDataflow_cpp.h
index f51be21..db93ec8 100644
--- a/Moira/MoiraDataflow_cpp.h
+++ b/Moira/MoiraDataflow_cpp.h
@@ -1253,6 +1253,11 @@ Moira::completeBusError(BusError &e, u32 addr)
         e.stackFrame.ssw = size | (fc & 7);
         if (!W) e.stackFrame.ssw |= SSW040::RW;
 
+        // The fault address is the first byte of the access, whichever of its
+        // bus transfers failed (MC68040UM 8.4.6.4); WB3A takes it too, so that
+        // a handler completing the write-back writes the whole operand there.
+        e.stackFrame.addr = addr & addrMask<Core::C68020>();
+
     } else {
 
         // On the 68020 and 68030, a fault in program space belongs to the
